From 36fdb2d6baf70750e52aab82bea01ca5cae04e60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:33:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(transitions): what takes no part in a motion stays
 in sight

The stage goes one level below floating windows and is left open over every window that stays put with
nothing crossing in front of it: a pinned call goes on playing, dialogs and panels no longer vanish for the
length of a motion, and a window kept in view is never buried under another's stand-in. The controller remembers what
each stage is playing, so a stand-in on its way gets no hole, one that was leaving goes on leaving, and whatever
changes the screen without a layout puts only the picture right (putMotionRight), never the arrangement. Stand-ins end where
their windows are, also after layout <line>, summon, move-to-display, a dock across displays and a move by somebody
else. A motion that is put right takes what is left of its time, at least 0.15 s. Whoever takes the stages down says
endMotions. Where macOS tiles the window that was let go, nothing is played. The focus ring's flash waits until the stage has
come down. windowPictures stays off.
