From f8773172b69618c155d545423ca40fd811261553 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:33:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(mac-shell): one run films, traces and judges the
 motion; the fake Mac records traces

shots-F02.sh looks at the look that ships first (colour and icon), then at what takes no part, at eight windows at 0.46 s
(one kept in view, one floating, one Arbor knows nothing about) in light and dark with macOS's tiling on and off, at pictures
of windows allowed and refused, and at the motion switched off. Each part records a trace and counts the frames each act gave
each window. arbor-fakemac wraps the seams in the recording decorators as the app does, so trace on and off can be
rehearsed on Linux, and takes the test windows' own form of open.
